---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Wordmark from "../components/Wordmark.astro";
import "../styles/tokens.css";
import "../styles/shell.css";
import "../styles/doc.css";
import "../styles/page.css";
---
<Base
  title={"Brand · Rabta"}
  description={"The Rabta wordmark: one outlined path in one colour. Its two colourways, the tile, clear space and the smallest it goes, the rules, and the files to use it."}
  route="/brand/"
  ogTitle={"The Rabta wordmark"}
  ogDescription={"One word, one path, one colour. The wordmark, its two colourways, the tile, and the files to use it."}
>
  <div class="wrap page-head">
    <p class="page-head__label">Brand</p>
    <h1>The word is the mark.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Rabta has no symbol. It is written: five rounded lowercase letters as one
      outlined path, in one colour. This page is the wordmark: the two grounds
      it sits on, the tile, the rules, and the files to use it.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- The wordmark, live. Each plate brings it in when it scrolls into view
       and again on request. -->
  <section class="band" aria-labelledby="wordmark-title">
    <div class="band__inner">
      <div class="band__body">
        <h2 id="wordmark-title">One path, one colour.</h2>
        <p>
          The wordmark is a single outlined path, so it never depends on a font
          being installed and never changes shape between machines. It takes
          the text colour of whatever it sits on: ink on paper, paper on ink.
          The ember is never on the letters.
        </p>

        <div class="specimen">
          <div class="specimen__plate">
            <Wordmark id="specimen-ink" data-mark="draw" label="The Rabta wordmark, paper on ink" />
            <button class="button button--small specimen__replay" type="button" data-mark-replay aria-controls="specimen-ink">Show it again</button>
          </div>
          <div class="specimen__plate specimen__plate--paper paper">
            <Wordmark id="specimen-paper" data-mark="draw" label="The Rabta wordmark, ink on paper" />
            <button class="button button--small specimen__replay" type="button" data-mark-replay aria-controls="specimen-paper">Show it again</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band" aria-labelledby="name-title">
    <div class="band__inner">
      <div class="band__body">
        <h2 id="name-title">Rabta is رابطة: a bond, a link, the thing that ties things together.</h2>
        <p>
          The product is exactly that. Your tools each remember their own piece
          of a task; Rabta is the bond between them. The name is pronounced
          RAHB-tah. In running text it is a word like any other; the wordmark
          is for the places the brand signs its name.
        </p>
        <div class="name" aria-hidden="true">
          <div>
            <p class="name__word">Rabta</p>
            <p>In running text: Inter, weight 560, the face of everything else on this site. This is the name in type, not the wordmark.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="name__word name__word--arabic">رابطة</p>
            <p>The name in its own alphabet, set in Reem Kufi, for the name only. It sits under the wordmark as a signature, never as decoration.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="mono muted foot-note">
          Three faces on this site, all under the SIL Open Font License and
          each shipped beside its licence: Inter for everything, Reem Kufi for
          the name only, Geist Mono for what is checkable: receipts,
          terminals, code, hashes, paths.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band" aria-labelledby="ways-title">
    <div class="band__inner">
      <div class="band__body">
        <h2 id="ways-title">Ink on paper, paper on ink, and the tile.</h2>
        <p>
          Two colourways and nothing in between: ink on a paper surface, paper
          on an ink surface. Inlined, the wordmark takes the text colour on its
          own. The tile is the ink wordmark on an ember squircle, for the Dock,
          the favicon and any avatar: the one place the ember and the letters
          share a frame, and even there the letters stay ink.
        </p>
        <div class="ways">
          <div class="way" data-reveal>
            <div class="way__plate way__plate--paper"><img class="way__wordmark" src="/assets/brand/wordmark-ink.svg" width="961" height="293" alt="" /></div>
            <h3>Ink on paper</h3>
            <a class="link link--arrow" href="/assets/brand/wordmark-ink.svg" download>Download SVG</a>
          </div>
          <div class="way" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="60">
            <div class="way__plate way__plate--ink"><img class="way__wordmark" src="/assets/brand/wordmark-paper.svg" width="961" height="293" alt="" /></div>
            <h3>Paper on ink</h3>
            <a class="link link--arrow" href="/assets/brand/wordmark-paper.svg" download>Download SVG</a>
          </div>
          <div class="way" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="120">
            <div class="way__plate way__plate--paper"><img class="way__wordmark" src="/assets/brand/wordmark.svg" width="961" height="293" alt="" /></div>
            <h3>One colour, yours</h3>
            <a class="link link--arrow" href="/assets/brand/wordmark.svg" download>Download SVG, currentColor</a>
          </div>
          <div class="way" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="180">
            <div class="way__plate way__plate--paper"><img src="/assets/brand/favicon.svg" width="100" height="100" alt="" /></div>
            <h3>The tile</h3>
            <a class="link link--arrow" href="/assets/brand/favicon.svg" download>Download SVG</a>
          </div>
          <div class="way" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="240">
            <div class="way__plate way__plate--paper"><img src="/assets/brand/icon-512.png" width="512" height="512" alt="" /></div>
            <h3>The tile at 512</h3>
            <a class="link link--arrow" href="/assets/brand/icon-512.png" download>Download PNG</a>
          </div>
          <div class="way" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="300">
            <div class="way__plate way__plate--ink"><img class="way__card" src="/assets/brand/og-cover.png" width="1200" height="630" alt="" /></div>
            <h3>The social card</h3>
            <a class="link link--arrow" href="/assets/brand/og-cover.png" download>Download PNG</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band" aria-labelledby="space-title">
    <div class="band__inner">
      <div class="band__body">
        <h2 id="space-title">Clear space, and the smallest it goes.</h2>
        <p>
          Keep one cap height of clear space on every side: the height of the
          b, from its top to the baseline. Nothing else sits inside that box.
          Never set the wordmark below 22px tall, and never the tile below
          16px. Under those, write the name.
        </p>
        <div class="construction" data-reveal>
          <div class="clear" aria-hidden="true"><Wordmark /></div>
          <p>The dashed line is the clear space: the wordmark, plus one cap height on every side.</p>
          <div class="floor" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="floor__item"><Wordmark /><span>22px, the floor</span></div>
            <div class="floor__item"><img src="/assets/brand/favicon.svg" width="16" height="16" alt="" /><span>16px, the tile's floor</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band" aria-labelledby="never-title">
    <div class="band__inner">
      <div class="band__body">
        <h2 id="never-title">Never.</h2>
        <dl class="denials">
          <div data-reveal>
            <dt>Outline it</dt>
            <dd>The letters are filled shapes. A stroke around them is a different, thinner word.</dd>
          </div>
          <div data-reveal data-reveal-delay="60">
            <dt>Rotate it</dt>
            <dd>It reads on a baseline, and only there.</dd>
          </div>
          <div data-reveal data-reveal-delay="120">
            <dt>Stretch it</dt>
            <dd>Scale both axes together, always. The proportions are the wordmark.</dd>
          </div>
          <div data-reveal data-reveal-delay="180">
            <dt>Put it in a circle</dt>
            <dd>The tile is a squircle, and the tile is the only container it has.</dd>
          </div>
          <div data-reveal data-reveal-delay="240">
            <dt>Add a shadow</dt>
            <dd>Or a glow, a gradient, or a second colour. It is flat, in one colour, on a flat surface.</dd>
          </div>
          <div data-reveal data-reveal-delay="300">
            <dt>Set the name in a typeface instead</dt>
            <dd>Where the wordmark belongs, use the path. Type is for the name in running text.</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band" aria-labelledby="palette-title">
    <div class="band__inner">
      <div class="band__body">
        <h2 id="palette-title">Paper, ink, one ember.</h2>
        <p>
          Both worlds are neutral with a cool cast, so a screenshot of the dark
          app sits naturally on the light site. The ember is spent once per
          view: on the primary action, or on the live thing, never both, and
          never on the wordmark.
        </p>
        <div class="swatches">
          <div class="swatch" data-reveal><div class="swatch__color swatch__color--paper-0"></div><div class="swatch__meta"><b>Paper</b><span>#FFFFFF</span></div></div>
          <div class="swatch" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="40"><div class="swatch__color swatch__color--paper-1"></div><div class="swatch__meta"><b>Paper, alt</b><span>#F5F5F7</span></div></div>
          <div class="swatch" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="80"><div class="swatch__color swatch__color--ink-0"></div><div class="swatch__meta"><b>Ink</b><span>#0A0B0E</span></div></div>
          <div class="swatch" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="120"><div class="swatch__color swatch__color--ink-1"></div><div class="swatch__meta"><b>Ink, raised</b><span>#14161B</span></div></div>
          <div class="swatch" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="160"><div class="swatch__color swatch__color--ember"></div><div class="swatch__meta"><b>Ember</b><span>#FF6B2C</span></div></div>
          <div class="swatch" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="200"><div class="swatch__color swatch__color--ember-deep"></div><div class="swatch__meta"><b>Ember, deep</b><span>#C2501B</span></div></div>
          <div class="swatch" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="240"><div class="swatch__color swatch__color--text"></div><div class="swatch__meta"><b>Text</b><span>#0E0F12</span></div></div>
          <div class="swatch" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="280"><div class="swatch__color swatch__color--text-mute"></div><div class="swatch__meta"><b>Text, muted</b><span>#4A4D57</span></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band--close" aria-labelledby="motion-title">
    <div class="band__inner">
      <div class="band__body">
        <h2 id="motion-title">Everything that comes back settles the same way.</h2>
        <p>
          One settling curve for anything that comes to rest, and one spring
          for the moment something lands. The wordmark arrives in just over a
          second: it rises into place and settles on the spring. A window
          returns by rising into place; a headline rises from behind its own
          baseline; a restore completes with the ember. Under reduced motion,
          all of it collapses to a fade, and the wordmark is simply there.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
